{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 34, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "Stepping off the plane in Tokyo, the first thing that hits you is the electric hum of the city. My recent trip to Japan was a perfect blend of ancient tradition and futuristic innovation. We started in the neon-drenched streets of Shibuya, watching the famous scramble crossing where thousands of people move in a synchronized dance. The energy is palpable, a stark contrast to the serene silence of the bamboo forests in Kyoto.\n\nOur days were a whirlwind of sensory experiences. We visited the towering Senso-ji Temple in Asakusa, where the scent of incense mingled with the chatter of locals. Later, we wandered through the quiet gardens of the Imperial Palace, finding peace amidst the urban sprawl. One of the highlights was the food. From steaming bowls of ramen in tiny alleyway shops to exquisite kaiseki dining, every meal was a masterpiece. The attention to detail in Japanese cuisine is unmatched; even a simple piece of sushi feels like an art form.\n\nThe train system was another wonder. Punctual to the second, the Shinkansen bullet train zipped us across the country, offering breathtaking views of Mount Fuji on clear days. The efficiency and politeness of the people made navigating a foreign country effortless. A simple bow and a warm \"arigato gozaimasu\" opened doors everywhere.\n\nAs the trip ended, I realized Japan isn't just a destination; it's an experience that rewires your appreciation for the world. The harmony between the old and the new, the respect for nature, and the relentless pursuit of perfection make it a place you never truly leave behind. I'm already planning my return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ste", "logprob": -2.5155702}, {"token": "pping", "logprob": -1.192093e-07}, {"token": " off", "logprob": -0.042336438}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " plane", "logprob": -0.019662924}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.00092573086}